=================== C'S SHAPE, WITH LINE NUMBERS ===================

  product_coding_loop.c:3374  av1_cost_calc_cfl(...)          <- one alpha
  product_coding_loop.c:3413    svt_cfl_predict_lbd(...)      <- U, INDIRECT
  product_coding_loop.c:3436    svt_aom_residual_kernel(...)
  product_coding_loop.c:3448    svt_aom_full_loop_uv(..., 0)
  product_coding_loop.c:3487    svt_cfl_predict_lbd(...)      <- V, INDIRECT
  common_dsp_rtcd.h:73        RTCD_EXTERN void(*svt_cfl_predict_lbd)(...)
  common_dsp_rtcd.c:494       SET_AVX2(svt_cfl_predict_lbd, _c, _avx2)
  ASM_AVX2/cfl_avx2.c:38      svt_cfl_predict_lbd_avx2

and the kernel body (`cfl_avx2.c:16-31`, `predict_unclipped`):

    ac_sign = sign_epi16(alpha_sign, ac_q3)              // sign(a)*sign(ac)
    mag     = mulhrs_epi16(abs_epi16(ac_q3), |alpha|<<9)
    res     = add_epi16(sign_epi16(mag, ac_sign), dc_q0)
    ... packus_epi16 -> u8 (the unsigned saturate IS the 0..255 clamp)

`mulhrs(x, y) = (x*y + 16384) >> 15`, so with `y = |alpha| << 9` the numerator
is `512 * (|ac|*|alpha| + 32)` and `mag = (|ac|*|alpha| + 32) >> 6` EXACTLY —
C's round-half-away-from-zero by 6, 16 i16 lanes at a time, no i32 widening.
Two further shapes worth naming: C's `dc_q0` is `_mm_set1_epi16(*pred)`, a
SCALAR broadcast of `pred[0]` (`pred_stride` is `(void)`-cast unused), and it
walks `pred_buf_q3` a whole 8- or 16-lane row at a time regardless of `width`.

WHAT THE PORT WAS DOING. The landed branch-free scalar loop
(`cfl_branchfree_2026-09-05`) computed the same value in i32, and on the
x86-64 BASELINE that is expensive: LLVM cannot know `alpha_q3` fits in 16
bits, so the multiply became a `pmuludq` + four `pshufd` quartet per FOUR
lanes (14 instructions for 8 elements), then the sign/round dance in i32
lanes, then `packssdw`+`packuswb`. Disassembled at
`svtav1_dsp::intra_pred::cfl_predict_lbd` in the base binary: ~45 SSE2
instructions per 8 elements plus ~20 of per-row bounds checks.

=================== WHAT LANDED (three chunks, one commit) ===================

1. **The kernel** (`svtav1-dsp/src/cfl_kernel.rs`, new). C's algorithm, one
   `#[arcane]` arm per tier reached by `incant!(..., [v3, neon, scalar])`:
   x86 `_mm256_mulhrs_epi16` (16 lanes) / `_mm_mulhrs_epi16` (8 and 4),
   aarch64 `vqrdmulhq_s16` (which computes `sat((2ab + 0x8000) >> 16)` =
   `(ab + 16384) >> 15`, the same value), the scalar arm = the existing
   branch-free core verbatim. The sign is applied as `(x ^ m) - m` with
   `m = (ac >> 15) ^ alpha_neg` rather than as C's two `sign_epi16`s: one
   instruction more on x86, but the SAME expression on both ISAs, and NEON has
   no `sign_epi16`. The `pred` term is loaded PER ELEMENT
   (`_mm256_cvtepu8_epi16` / `vmovl_u8`), not broadcast from `pred[0]` as C
   does — the port does not assume the DC base is uniform.
   Emitted inner loop (16 lanes, verified with objdump):
   `vmovdqu / vpsraw / vpxor / vpabsw / vpmulhrsw / vpxor / vpsubw /
    vpmovzxbw / vpaddw / vpackuswb / vmovdqu` + LLVM's own clamp pair.

2. **The per-alpha buffer hoist** (`leaf_funnel/cfl.rs`). `plane_cost` did
   `vec![0u8; cw*chh]` on EVERY alpha trial — `callcount_realimg_2026-09-04`
   item B names this exact site at 211,831 callocs on photo_cid p2 against
   20,754 calls to `md_cfl_rd_pick_alpha`. One buffer per SEARCH now.
   `cfl_predict_lbd` writes every byte of it (`dst_stride == width == cw` over
   all `chh` rows), so reuse cannot carry a stale value; `md_cfl_alpha_search`
   took `impl FnMut` to allow it. This is the LARGER half of the Ir win.

3. **The alpha loop inside one `#[arcane]` per tier** — the chunk this task
   was dispatched to test. **It does not do what it was meant to do, and it is
   in the tree anyway; read the next section before citing it.**

