=================== THE CHUNK THAT DID NOT DO WHAT IT SAYS ===================

The dispatch brief, and `archmage/docs/PERFORMANCE.md`'s rule ("enter
`#[arcane]` once from non-SIMD code and put the loop INSIDE"; the boundary
costs 4x on a simple add and 6.2x on DCT-8), predicted that wrapping the WHOLE
alpha loop in one `#[arcane]` per tier would let `plane_cost` — and through it
`cfl_predict_lbd` and `tx_unit` — inline into the `#[target_feature]` region
and stop crossing the boundary 211,831 times a frame.

**MEASURED: the closure does not inline.** In the built binary
`svtav1_encoder::leaf_funnel::cfl::md_cfl_rd_pick_alpha::{closure#0}` is still
its own out-of-line symbol, 654,113,773 inclusive Ir on photo_cid p2 and
2,368,166,396 on photo_clic — i.e. the boundary is crossed exactly as often as
before and `tx_unit` never enters the AVX2 region. `#[arcane]` did fire (three
`__arcane_md_cfl_alpha_search_impl_v3::<...>` monomorphisations exist, one per
closure type); LLVM simply declined to inline a body that large.

And it is Ir-WORSE, on both cells, measured against the same base
(k+hoist -> k+hoist+arcane):
    photo_cid   45,916,743,174 -> 45,915,708,369  (-0.002 %, a null)
                the CFL subtree 686,190,961 -> 688,062,356  (+1.9 M)
    photo_clic  45,185,097,146 -> 45,191,716,532  (+0.015 %)
                the CFL subtree 2,445,276,387 -> 2,450,070,566  (+4.8 M)

It is in the tree because the campaign DECIDES ON WALL CLOCK, and on wall clock
it wins, consistently, on four of five cells with non-overlapping spans
(21 paired rounds each, ident=Y, same quiet box):
    photo_clic 512 p2  **1.010x** (0.9863-0.9950)
    photo_cid  512 p2  **1.008x** (0.9887-0.9932)
    gradient   512 p2    1.005x  (0.9931-0.9978)
    gradient   256 p2    1.002x  (0.9944-0.9994)
    gradient   512 p6    1.001x  (0.9926-1.0029 — straddles; a null)

That is a code-LAYOUT / register-allocation effect of the extra frame, and it
is the exact MIRROR of the variant `cfl_branchfree_2026-09-05` rejected (fewer
instructions, slower everywhere). Applying that record's own rule symmetrically
means keeping this one. **But do not cite it as evidence for the inlining
model** — the model predicts a large Ir DROP from removing 211,831 boundary
crossings, and what was measured is a small Ir RISE with the crossings intact.

=================== TWO CORRECTIONS TO THE STANDING RECORD ===================

1. **`cfl_branchfree_2026-09-05`'s diagnosis of its own rejected variant is
   NOT supported.** It read: "an `#[arcane]` arm is an out-of-line
   `target_feature` function, so the dispatch takes the call out of the
   closure and out of the inliner's reach", and it concluded "a HAND-WRITTEN
   intrinsics kernel that the inliner can still fold into the alpha closure is
   the untried next step ... it must be inlinable to win." The kernel that
   landed here IS an `#[arcane]` arm behind `incant!`, is NOT inlined into the
   closure, and wins 1.017x / 1.018x on the photos and 1.010-1.013x on the
   gradient — where the rejected variant lost 0.993x. The variable that
   changed is the ARITHMETIC, not the linkage. The oracle says the same: C's
   kernel is reached through a function pointer and costs 99 Ir.
2. The record's "12x per call" is superseded twice over: it was 6.48x on this
   base (the branch-free scalar loop had already halved it) and is 4.15x now.

=================== WHAT WAS MEASURED AND REVERTED ===================

**Row-iterator slicing in the kernel — a REGRESSION, reverted, so nobody
retries it.** Replacing `pred_buf_q3[j*CFL_BUF_LINE .. +width]` (three
multiply-and-compare bounds checks per row) with `chunks(stride).take(height)
.map(|r| &r[..width])` iterators, on the theory that per-row overhead dominates
a 4x4 chroma block, made the KERNEL slower by instruction count on both cells:
photo_cid 96,103,494 -> 111,029,393 (+15.5 %), photo_clic 232,434,738 ->
267,887,105 (+15.3 %). The direct indexing is what LLVM hoists best here. Both
forms are in the .tsv as `k+hoist` and `k+iter+hoist`.

=================== EXACTNESS ===================

Every SIMD arm is pinned against `cfl_predict_lbd_core` by TWO tests, both
inside `for_each_token_permutation` with the `PermutationReport` CONSUMED
(`warnings.is_empty()` + `permutations_run >= 2`, so the sweep cannot silently
degenerate to the native tier — `rust/CLAUDE.md`'s silent-coverage hazard):
  * `cfl_simd_matches_scalar_for_every_alpha_and_ac` — EXHAUSTIVE: all 33
    `alpha_q3` values `cfl_idx_to_alpha` can produce (0 and magnitudes 1..=16
    either sign) x all 65,535 `i16` `ac_q3` values except `i16::MIN`, through
    the 16-, 8- and 4-wide paths at three `pred` values. 6.5 M comparisons.
  * `cfl_simd_matches_scalar_over_the_reachable_domain` — every width 1..=32
    (so every `width % 4` tail) x three heights.
The `i16::MIN` exclusion is the ONE divergence and it is C's:
`_mm256_abs_epi16(i16::MIN)` and `vabsq_s16(i16::MIN)` both return `i16::MIN`,
so C's own AVX2 and NEON kernels have it too (and disagree with each other
there). It is unreachable regardless — `cfl_luma_subsampling_420` writes
`2 * (sum of four u8) <= 2040` and `cfl_subtract_average` subtracts a mean of
that same buffer, so `|ac_q3| <= 2040`. Stated in the module header.
The pre-existing exhaustive `cfl_branch_free_rounding_matches_the_branchy_form`
(2,162,720 pairs) is untouched and still runs.

