=================== MEMORY (CPU was the priority; report it anyway) ===================

Nothing here allocates more per frame; chunk 2 allocates ~191,000 times LESS
and holds one <= 1 KiB buffer (`cw*chh`, at most 32x32) across a search
instead. Measured, not argued, with `tools/mem_bisect.sh` (both binaries
round-robin in ONE run, so box drift lands on both equally):

x86_64 r7900x, peak HEAP (heaptrack, LIVE malloc'd bytes), one encode each:
    2048 inter  101.78 M -> 101.78 M   UNCHANGED
    2048 still   61.06 M ->  61.06 M   UNCHANGED
x86_64 r7900x, peak RSS (`/usr/bin/time -v`), 2048 inter, 15 rounds:
    median 104,472 -> 104,396 KiB (min 103,972 -> 104,032, max 104,740 ->
    104,892) — the distributions overlap completely. A NULL.
aarch64 Mac, peak RSS (`/usr/bin/time -l`), 15 rounds inter / 11 still:
    2048 inter  median 140,224 -> 140,160 KiB (min 140,160 -> 138,560,
                max 149,392 -> 159,008) — overlapping, and the MIN went down.
                A NULL: **the aarch64 inter arm is not pushed anywhere**, which
                is the arm the memory goal is stated against.
    2048 still  median  72,640 ->  72,672 KiB (min 72,592 -> 72,624,
                max 74,736 -> 72,768) — overlapping. A NULL.
Every row above encoded (rc 0, obu 139,761 B inter / 70,893 B still) — no
REFUSED cell was averaged in.

=================== WHAT IS AND IS NOT ESTABLISHED ===================

ESTABLISHED: C's call shape, with line numbers, and that it is an INDIRECT
out-of-line call per alpha per plane; the Ir on three contents at p2; the
kernel's per-call cost against C's on two contents; the wall clock on six cells
at 21 paired rounds each on a quiet box; that both SIMD arms equal the scalar
core over the whole reachable `(alpha_q3, ac_q3)` domain; that the row-iterator
form is worse; that the arcane-alpha-loop chunk does NOT inline the closure.
NOT ESTABLISHED: that this is as fast as C's kernel — it is still 4.15x C's Ir
per call, and the residual is per-ROW overhead (three bounds checks and a slice
setup per row, which on a 4x4 chroma block dwarfs the 4 elements of work) plus
the 31-Ir `incant!` frame. C pays neither: it walks a whole 8- or 16-lane row
regardless of `width` and indexes with pointers. Also not established: any
preset but 2 for the Ir (p6/p10 unmeasured), any qp but 40, 10-bit
(`cfl_predict_hbd` and the bd10 `plane_cost10` closure — which still allocates
`vec![0u16; cw*chh]` per alpha trial — are both UNTOUCHED and are the obvious
next chunk), and the inter arm.
